---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <Header lang="en" client:load />
  
  <main class="flex-grow bg-brand-bg pt-12 pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-12 bg-white p-8 md:p-12 shadow-sm rounded-lg">
      <h1 class="font-cinzel text-2xl md:text-3xl text-brand-text font-bold mb-8 text-center uppercase tracking-wider">Privacy Policy</h1>
      
      <div class="space-y-6 text-brand-text/80 leading-relaxed text-xs md:text-sm">
        <section>
          <p class="mb-3">At Hotel Plaza San Antonio EIRL we value your privacy and are deeply committed to protecting your personal data. This Privacy Policy outlines how we collect, use, and share information about you when you visit our website https://www.hotelplazasanantonio.com.pe and utilize our hotel services.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-brand-text mb-3">1. Information We Collect</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">We may collect the following categories of personal information:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Contact Information:</strong> including full name, email address, telephone number, and home or postal address.</li>
            <li><strong>Booking Information:</strong> details regarding your reservation stays, arrival and departure dates, room preferences, and special guest requests.</li>
            <li><strong>Payment Information:</strong> credit or debit card details, or alternative payment data provided to guarantee or prepay your reservations.</li>
            <li><strong>Technical Information:</strong> IP addresses, browser types, operating systems, and automated browsing behavior across our website.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        
        <section>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-brand-text mb-3">2. Use of Information</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">We process and utilize your personal data for the following specific purposes:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-2">
            <li>Managing, confirming, and processing room reservations and associated hospitality services.</li>
            <li>Communicating directly regarding upcoming stays, sending essential arrival details and confirmations.</li>
            <li>Answering inquiries, customer service requests, or submitted comments and feedback.</li>
            <li>Enhancing internal services and tailoring guest hospitality experiences during stays.</li>
            <li>Sending occasional promotional communications or newsletters (only where prior explicit consent was granted).</li>
            <li>Complying with statutory accounting, migration, and local regulatory obligations.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        
        <section>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-brand-text mb-3">3. Information Sharing</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">We never sell, rent, or distribute personal guest information to unauthorized third parties for marketing purposes. Data sharing only takes place under these circumstances:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-3 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Service Providers:</strong> We share essential operational details with contracted technology vendors hosting reservation engines or payment infrastructure (such as Sleep and Go S.L.), always operating under strict data security agreements.</li>
            <li><strong>Legal Requirements:</strong> We may disclose guest records if strictly required by formal regulatory mandates, judiciary subpoenas, police investigation, or defending legitimate hotel rights.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-brand-text mb-3">4. Data Security</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">We implement industry-standard organizational, technological, and procedural administrative security measures designed to safeguard all personal data against accidental loss, unauthorized access, illicit disclosure, or alteration. However, please remember no electronic data transmission over public internet networks is guaranteed completely immune to external interception.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-brand-text mb-3">5. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">You possess legal rights to access, amend, cancel, or formally oppose further operational handling of personal data stored in our hospitality registers. To assert these data rights, please contact management via email at <strong>hplazasanantonio@gmail.com</strong> or via telephone at <strong>+51 (054) 220502</strong> along with an official identity verification document.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-brand-text mb-3">6. Policy Updates</h2>
          <p class="mb-3">We reserve the right to revise or amend this Privacy Policy whenever operational procedures change. Revised provisions immediately take effect upon digital publication across this web portal.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  
  <Footer lang="en" />
</Layout>
